{
  "description": "Preserve Self-EvolveRec’s diagnostic interface while adapting its probes to the corrected BERT4Rec model. Return measured metrics with explicit definitions and generate an interpretation prompt grounded in those measurements.",
  "motivation": "Reliable diagnosis requires probes that match the trained architecture and available data. This adapter supports model improvement without inventing unavailable attributes or changing the benchmark selection criterion.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Access the actual trained network through view.model and preserve item_emb, log2feats(sequence), predict_score(features, items), and the host’s data interfaces. Handle left padding by locating the final nonpadding position rather than using count-1. Respect BERT4Rec’s reserved mask token, masked-target training, and appended-mask inference without target leakage. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; treat unavailable review fields and simulator traits as unobserved. Produce full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category. Select models using macro validation HR@10 across all four categories. Maintain one independently trained checkpoint per category and consistent training and embedded prediction architectures.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        set view.model to evaluation mode\n        with gradients disabled:\n            for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n                identify valid tokens and masked targets using BERT4Rec conventions\n                compute applicable probes through the preserved ModelView interfaces\n                accumulate measurements with explicit denominators\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: measured_results, metric_definitions: definitions_and_availability}\n\ndiagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    return prompt containing measured metrics, definitions, availability limits,\n           and instructions to distinguish observations from hypotheses",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Connects architecture-aware diagnosis to a controlled recommendation benchmark.",
    "negative": "Primarily an interface and measurement specification rather than a new learning algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support reproducible diagnosis and targeted improvements across sequential model architectures.",
    "negative": "Predictive value depends on the chosen probes; no diagnostic results or validation gains are supplied."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces and available data are clearly specified.",
    "negative": "Correct masking, padding, metric aggregation, and predictor consistency require careful implementation."
  }
}
